  "uncertainty_note": "Bands and errors are the plotted values. See the figure caption for confidence level and estimator.",
  "data_note": "Exact numerical artist inputs in plotted units; no values have been digitised from a PDF or recomputed from curves.",
  "caption_latex": "Local and remote spin--cavity correlations in the three-spin weak-end chain. Each panel compares feedback off, feedback on the middle spin, and independent drive noise on that spin. With $q_j=(a_j+a_j^\\dagger)/\\sqrt{2}$ and $p_j=(a_j-a_j^\\dagger)/(i\\sqrt{2})$, the panels show {(a)} local covariance magnitude $|\\langle\\sigma_2^x q_2\\rangle_c|$, {(b)} middle-spin/end-cavity covariance $|\\langle\\sigma_2^y p_1\\rangle_c|$, {(c)} end-spin/middle-cavity covariance $|\\langle\\sigma_1^y p_2\\rangle_c|$, {(d)} local covariance $|\\langle\\sigma_2^y p_2\\rangle_c|$, {(e)} mutual information between spin 2 and cavity 2, in bits, and {(f)} their entanglement negativity. The subscript $c$ denotes subtraction of the product of means; mixed covariances are displayed as magnitudes. {The plots in} {(b--d)} share a vertical scale. Feedback changes the remote pairs without a comparably large sustained increase in local information or entanglement. Solid cap-five and dotted cap-four master-equation curves test the photon cutoff; these deterministic controls are not HOPS and have no sampling bands. The largest cap changes are below $6.0\\times10^{-4}$ for mixed covariances, $3.4\\times10^{-4}$ for negativity and $2.2\\times10^{-4}$ bits for mutual information."
}
